WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Speaker 1: All right, a big story breaking this&nbsp;
morning about the January 6th investigation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:10.320
it happens to be really bad news for the Trump&nbsp;
family. Eric Trump as well as Kimberly Guilfoyle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:16.640
phone records have been subpoenaed and reportedly&nbsp;
obtained by the Jan. six committee, again pushing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:22.400
forward into the inner circle around Trump and&nbsp;
theoretically, eventually to Trump himself. Eric&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:30.080
Trump is one of Trump's sons. Kimberly Guilfoyle&nbsp;
is the fiancee of Don Jr., and their records now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:36.400
are becoming part of the investigation. CNN&nbsp;
reporting exclusive Eric Trump and Kimberly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:43.520
Guilfoyle phone records subpoenaed by the January&nbsp;
six committee. The House Committee investigating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:51.280
the Jan. six attack on the Capitol, has subpoenaed&nbsp;
and obtained records of phone numbers associated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:56.560
with one of former Trump's children, Eric Trump,&nbsp;
as well as Kimberly Guilfoyle. It appears to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:01.680
the first time the select committee has issued&nbsp;
a subpoena that targeted a member of the Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:07.280
family and what marks a significant escalation&nbsp;
of the investigation into Trump's role in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:12.720
January 6th insurrection. The decision to subpoena&nbsp;
communication records involving the Trump family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:19.920
underscores the aggressive tack the committee is&nbsp;
taking as it races to complete its investigation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:25.440
while battling Trump in court over access to&nbsp;
documents. The phone records obtained by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:31.120
committee are part of a new round of call detail&nbsp;
records. These records provide the committee with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:36.000
logs that show incoming and outgoing calls,&nbsp;
including date, time and length of calls.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.000
The records show a log of text messages,&nbsp;
but not necessarily the substance or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.400
content. This is fascinating because this&nbsp;
is this is that the so-called metadata&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:52.240
and one of the things that we learned from Edward&nbsp;
Snowden's exposures are about practices of bulk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:55.920
metadata collection and one of the things&nbsp;
that the right has been very quick to say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:01.040
some on the right who want to defend government&nbsp;
surveillance. Not it, not all of them do. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:05.680
libertarian minded ones don't, but sometimes they&nbsp;
say, Listen, this is just metadata. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:10.640
it's not actually the substance and the kind.&nbsp;
It's not recordings of calls or the text of text&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:17.280
messages. Well, that's what's here. That's what&nbsp;
we're talking about here. And they are flipping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:23.760
out because they have done this with regard to&nbsp;
Eric Trump and Kimberly Guilfoyle. Both Eric Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:29.520
and Guilfoyle played prominent roles in Trump's&nbsp;
Stop the Steal efforts, including Guilt Guilfoyle&nbsp;&nbsp;

